<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ivrea</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Eporedia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ivrea is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piedmont">Piedmont</a>, north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dora-baltea">Dora Baltea</a> where it leaves the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alps">Alps</a>. Founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> in 100 BCE as the colony of Eporedia to guard the Alpine routes, it was later the seat of the March of Ivrea, whose rulers Berengar II and Arduin became kings of Italy. In the 20th century it was the home of the Olivetti company, and its industrial town is a World Heritage Site.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ivrea.jpg" alt="Ivrea" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Valerio Bozzolan · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Linux_Day_Ivrea_2021_-_visione_d%27insieme_da_Piazza_Rondolino_direzione_Ovest_naviglio.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
